    {
     "start_timestamp": "2026-08-19T04:20:02.000000Z",
     "stop_timestamp": "2026-08-19T04:20:13.126000Z",
     "type": "text",
     "text": "General outline (confirm on the California DMV site, rules change):\n\n- **Deadline**: California expects you to register within **20 days** of becoming a resident (e.g., taking a job, signing a lease, or otherwise establishing residency).\n- **Driver's license**: new residents are expected to get a CA license within 10 days.\n\n**Process**\n1. **Smog check** at a licensed station (most vehicles need one when first registered in CA).\n2. **Vehicle verification** at the DMV or by a licensed verifier (they check the VIN).\n3. Submit the **Application for Title or Registration**, your VA title (or lienholder info if financed), VA registration, proof of insurance, smog certificate.\n4. Pay fees (registration, license fee based on vehicle value, possibly use tax if the car was bought recently out of state).\n\nMake an appointment; SF DMV offices are busy.\n\nAlso update your car insurance to the SF address. Rates will change, and an out-of-state policy can be a problem after you've moved.",
     "citations": []
    }
   ],
